          "changeMeaning": "Display introductory title and show linear geometry model (steric number 2) with labels.",
          "narration": "Welcome to the VSEPR Theory lab. Valence Shell Electron Pair Repulsion theory predicts 3D molecular structures based on the idea that electron domains repel each other and stay as far apart as possible. Here, we see a steric number of 2, which creates a Linear electron-domain geometry with a perfect 180-degree bond angle."
        },
        {
