                {
                  "componentType": "textMeshPro",
                  "text": "Steric Number: 3\\nGeometry: Trigonal Planar\\nBond Angle: 120\u00b0",
                  "color": [
                    1,
                    1,
                    1,
                    1
                  ],
                  "fontSize": 28,
                  "wrapText": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Swap linear geometry model for trigonal planar (steric number 3).",
          "narration": "When the central atom has three electron domains, its steric number is 3. To minimize mutual repulsion, these three domains arrange themselves pointing toward the corners of an equilateral triangle. This forms a Trigonal Planar geometry with 120-degree bond angles."
        },
        {
