                  "text": "Steric Number: 4\\nGeometry: Tetrahedral\\nBond Angle: 109.5\u00b0",
                  "color": [
                    1,
                    1,
                    1,
                    1
                  ],
                  "fontSize": 28,
                  "wrapText": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Swap trigonal planar for tetrahedral geometry (steric number 4).",
          "narration": "With four electron domains, the steric number is 4. Rather than staying in a flat 2D plane at 90 degrees, the domains push out into three dimensions to achieve maximum separation. This produces a Tetrahedral geometry with characteristic 109.5-degree bond angles."
        },
