                  "text": "Steric Number: 5\\nGeometry: Trigonal Bipyramidal\\nAngles: 90\u00b0 (axial) & 120\u00b0 (equatorial)",
                  "color": [
                    1,
                    1,
                    1,
                    1
                  ],
                  "fontSize": 28,
                  "wrapText": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Swap tetrahedral for trigonal bipyramidal geometry (steric number 5).",
          "narration": "Five electron domains yield a steric number of 5, resulting in a Trigonal Bipyramidal geometry. This geometry features two distinct environments: axial domains pointing vertically at 90 degrees to the equator, and three equatorial domains lying in a horizontal plane 120 degrees apart from one another."
        },
