          "changeMeaning": "Swap trigonal bipyramidal for octahedral geometry (steric number 6).",
          "narration": "Finally, six electron domains form an Octahedral geometry. In this highly symmetric shape, all six positions are completely equivalent, and all adjacent domains sit at perfect 90-degree angles to one another. Observe how these five core structures minimize electrostatic repulsion for their respective steric numbers."
