              "components": [
                {
                  "componentType": "textMeshPro",
                  "text": "2 Lone Pairs (Maximum Repulsion)\\nWater (H2O)\\nBond Angle: 104.5\u00b0 (Bent)",
                  "color": [
                    1,
                    1,
                    1,
                    1
                  ],
                  "fontSize": 24,
                  "wrapText": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Display Water, showcasing 2 lone pairs squeezing the H-O-H bond angle even further.",
          "narration": "Now, look at Water. Water also has a steric number of 4, but features two lone pairs. These two large electron clouds repel each other and the O-H bonds strongly, pushing the remaining bonds even closer together. The H-O-H bond angle is compressed to 104.5 degrees, forming a Bent molecular geometry. Notice the clear trend: as lone pairs increase, bond angles decrease."
        }
