          "changeMeaning": "Display Phosphorus Pentafluoride (PF5) to show standard trigonal bipyramidal configuration.",
          "narration": "Let's move to real molecules with expanded octets. Phosphorus Pentafluoride, or PF5, has 5 bonding pairs and no lone pairs around Phosphorus. Its molecular geometry matches its electron-domain geometry: a perfect Trigonal Bipyramidal shape. The horizontal equatorial bonds are 120 degrees apart, while the vertical axial bonds form a 90-degree angle with the equator."
        },
