          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Display Sulfur Hexafluoride (SF6) to show octahedral configuration.",
          "narration": "Now consider Sulfur Hexafluoride, or SF6. With 6 bonding domains on the sulfur atom, its molecular geometry is Octahedral. All bond angles are exactly 90 degrees. Because there are no lone pairs, the structure is perfectly symmetrical, making SF6 a highly stable, nonpolar molecule despite its highly polar bonds."
        },
