          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Display Xenon Tetrafluoride (XeF4) showing axial lone pairs creating a square planar molecular shape.",
          "narration": "Finally, let's look at Xenon Tetrafluoride, or XeF4. Xenon has 6 electron domains: 4 bonding pairs and 2 lone pairs. To minimize mutual repulsion, the two bulky lone pairs position themselves as far apart as possible, at a 180-degree angle in the axial positions. This leaves the 4 fluorine atoms lying flat in the equatorial plane, resulting in a highly symmetrical Square Planar molecular geometry."
        },
