          "narration": "To master VSEPR theory, always follow these simple steps: First, draw the Lewis structure. Second, count the steric number by adding bonding domains and lone pairs. Third, determine the base electron-domain geometry. Fourth, place any lone pairs in positions that minimize repulsion. And finally, describe the resulting molecular shape. Thank you for completing the VSEPR lab!"
